
LogicBBS v1.0
-------------

lbbs.library is not included anywhere on the disks included in this package,
why?...

lbbs.library is resident, and included inside the mainprogram "LogicBBS".

You will always be sure, that the system is running, if you can open the
lbbs.library.

All structures and library calls will always be backwards compatible from
this version and up. So your tools will never be incompatible with newer
versions.

Structures may be extended in the future, but this will only be from the
end of a structure and either using a new APTR to the extended part,
 or just extended with extra bytes.

The support of /X doors will also be extended when we receive the last
information on the few calls, we still haven't covered.
Some calls are obsolete, and continues to be. As some function calls
through the /X msgport, are directly affecting internal datafiles of /X.

ARexx support of /X AIM utilities are already covered, with support of
 all known commands used thrugh ARexx. Don't forget the increased speed
 of AIM doors! .. We handle ARexx calls INTERNALLY, /X do it using EXTERNAL
 tools.

